# RBAC & Permissions

## Permission Checking

```php
public function __construct() {
    parent::__construct();
    require_module_access('employees');
    $this->load->model('Employee_model');
}
```

Views gate UI with `has_module_access('employees')` or granular keys like `employees_export`.

**AuthHook** reads `get_controller_module_access_map()` in `permission_helper.php` — do not duplicate keys in AuthHook.

## Adding New Permission Keys

See `.cursor/rules/new-feature-rbac-and-guide.mdc` for the full checklist (Permissions.php matrix, permission_helper map, view alignment, audit scripts).

## Data Scope

Use `data_scope` / `hierarchy_filter` helpers for org-wide vs scoped data. Admin tier (`role_id = 1` or admin group) sees all; others see scoped records only.

Apply scope in Model queries — never trust client-side role checks.

## Session Security

```php
// After login
$this->session->sess_regenerate(true);

// Logout
$this->session->sess_destroy();
```

## Audit Trail

Log permission-sensitive actions via `log_activity()` with user_id, action, module, record_id.

## Anti-Patterns

- Permission check mid-function instead of at start
- View button without matching controller gate
- Hardcoded role IDs (use constants)
- Storing secrets in session
- Forgetting data scope filter on list queries

## Office Meals Exception

Office Meals uses `meal_role_has()` / `require_meal_access()` — not `has_module_access()`. See new-feature-rbac rule section E.
